IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, section 5: "WITHOUT LAWFUL EXCUSE".
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Written from the text alone.
--
-- Sections 1 to 3 each say "without lawful excuse" and none defines it. Section 5
-- does two things: it deems a person to have a lawful excuse in two situations
-- (s 5(2)(a) consent, s 5(2)(b) protecting property), for some offences only
-- (s 5(1)); and it leaves every other lawful excuse and defence where it was
-- (s 5(2) opening words, s 5(5)). The Act does not say what those others are, so
-- whether one applies is a fact the person states (cda-nouns.l4:
-- `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)`).
--
-- Every belief in s 5(2) counts if it is honestly held, whether or not it is
-- justified (s 5(3)); the rules below read only `honestly held`.

§ `Section 5 -- "Without lawful excuse"`

§§ `5(1) -- the offences section 5 applies to`

-- src:25 | 5 “Without lawful excuse.”
-- src:26 | (1) This section applies to any offence under section 1(1) above and any offence under section 2 or 3 above other than one involving a threat by the person charged to destroy or damage property in a way which he knows is likely to endanger the life of another or involving an intent by the person charged to use or cause or permit the use of something in his custody or under his control so to destroy or damage property.
@ref s 5(1) (src:25-26)
GIVEN offence IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 5 applies to` offence MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `arson under section 1(1)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `arson under section 1(2)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under section 2(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offence under section 2(b)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under section 3(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offence under section 3(b)` THEN FALSE

§§ `5(2) -- treated as having a lawful excuse`

-- src:27 | (2) A person charged with an offence to which this section applies, shall, whether or not he would be treated for the purposes of this Act as having a lawful excuse apart from this subsection, be treated for those purposes as having a lawful excuse—
-- src:28 | (a) if at the time of the act or acts alleged to constitute the offence he believed that the person or persons whom he believed to be entitled to consent to the destruction of or damage to the property in question had so consented, or would have so consented to it if he or they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances; or
-- src:29 | (b) if he destroyed or damaged or threatened to destroy or damage the property in question or, in the case of a charge of an offence under section 3 above, intended to use or cause or permit the use of something to destroy or damage it, in order to protect property belonging to himself or another or a right or interest in property which was or which he believed to be vested in himself or another, and at the time of the act or acts alleged to constitute the offence he believed—
-- src:30 | (i) that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection; and
-- src:31 | (ii) that the means of protection adopted or proposed to be adopted were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances.
@ref s 5(2) (src:27-31)
GIVEN offence IS AN Offence
      facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 5(2) treats the accused as having a lawful excuse for` offence facts MEANS
        `section 5 applies to` offence
    AND (   `5(2)(a): the accused believed that consent had been given or would have been given` facts
         OR `5(2)(b): the accused acted to protect property, a right or an interest` facts)

-- (a): "he believed that the person or persons whom he believed to be entitled to
-- consent to the destruction of or damage to the property in question had so
-- consented, or would have so consented to it if he or they had known of the
-- destruction or damage and its circumstances". Either belief will do.
@ref s 5(2)(a) (src:28)
GIVEN facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`5(2)(a): the accused believed that consent had been given or would have been given` facts MEANS
        `a belief counts for the purposes of section 5` (facts's `belief that the persons believed to be entitled to consent had consented`)
    OR  `a belief counts for the purposes of section 5` (facts's `belief that those persons would have consented if they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances`)

-- (b): the purpose limb, then the two beliefs (i) and (ii), all three required.
@ref s 5(2)(b) (src:29-31)
GIVEN facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`5(2)(b): the accused acted to protect property, a right or an interest` facts MEANS
        `5(2)(b): the purpose was to protect property, or a right or interest in property that was or was believed to be vested in the accused or another` facts
    AND `5(2)(b)(i): the accused believed that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` facts
    AND `5(2)(b)(ii): the accused believed that the means of protection were or would be reasonable` facts

@ref s 5(2)(b) (src:29)
GIVEN facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`5(2)(b): the purpose was to protect property, or a right or interest in property that was or was believed to be vested in the accused or another` facts MEANS
        facts's `purpose of protecting property belonging to the accused or another`
    OR  (    `5(4): the purpose was to protect a right or interest in property` facts
         AND (   facts's `the right or interest was vested in the accused or another`
              OR `a belief counts for the purposes of section 5` (facts's `belief that the right or interest was vested in the accused or another`)))

@ref s 5(2)(b)(i) (src:30)
GIVEN facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`5(2)(b)(i): the accused believed that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` facts MEANS
    `a belief counts for the purposes of section 5` (facts's `belief that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection`)

-- (ii) is a belief that the means were reasonable, not a test of whether they were:
-- by s 5(3) an honestly held belief counts although it is not justified.
@ref s 5(2)(b)(ii) (src:31)
GIVEN facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`5(2)(b)(ii): the accused believed that the means of protection were or would be reasonable` facts MEANS
    `a belief counts for the purposes of section 5` (facts's `belief that the means of protection adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances`)

§§ `5(3) -- belief need only be honest`

-- src:32 | (3) For the purposes of this section it is immaterial whether a belief is justified or not if it is honestly held.
@ref s 5(3) (src:32)
GIVEN belief IS A Belief
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a belief counts for the purposes of section 5` belief MEANS
    belief's `honestly held`
    -- belief's `justified` is deliberately not read: s 5(3) makes it immaterial.

§§ `5(4) -- "right or interest in property"`

-- src:33 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2) above a right or interest in property includes any right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise.
@ref s 5(4) (src:33)
GIVEN facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`5(4): the purpose was to protect a right or interest in property` facts MEANS
        facts's `purpose of protecting a right or interest in property`
    OR  facts's `purpose of protecting a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise`

§§ `5(5) -- other defences are not cast in doubt`

-- src:34 | (5) This section shall not be construed as casting doubt on any defence recognised by law as a defence to criminal charges.
@ref s 5(5) (src:34)
GIVEN facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`5(5): a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2) is left in place` facts MEANS
    facts's `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)`

-- "Without lawful excuse" in sections 1 to 3: the lawful excuse that section 5(2)
-- deems (for the offences section 5(1) names) or that the law recognises apart from it.
@ref s 5(5) (src:34)
GIVEN offence IS AN Offence
      facts IS A `Lawful excuse facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the accused has a lawful excuse for` offence facts MEANS
        `section 5(2) treats the accused as having a lawful excuse for` offence facts
    OR  `5(5): a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2) is left in place` facts
